umented mixed-new-compiler/old-SDK limitation; do not treat local forced-guard simulation as real Swift 6.1 proof. Reuse unchanged validation evidence where justified and run focused adversarial checks. This review authorizes composition of the accepted delta into PR6 only; real hosted Xcode 16.4 CI and exact composed-head platform review remain mandatory before landing. Do not require PR6 landing for this candidate review, and do not fabricate older-toolchain evidence. No product/tooling edits, VPN operations, installations, routing changes or publication in the review run. Use real accept_cr or changes_requested with task-scoped verdict and live merged checklist. Control-root LOGBOOK additions are preserved in .temp/resume-20260916/logbook-preserved-07.patch plus a path-scoped stash; do not write the control-root LOGBOOK. Preserve producer .build for review reuse; report safely disposable caches after review. Operational config remains .temp/resume-20260916/task-board.config.json.\n\n\n### BUG-260916-20xt79_rework-prerequisite.md\n> Changed preconditions: reuse accepted validation fixture prerequisite\n\nRev1 automatic validation failed BEFORE mapper checks: untrusted local mise.toml and validation-contract-tests expected UI schemes missing from fixture. Evidence BUG-260916-20xt79_change-request_rev1-validation.log. Parent cancelled automatic unchanged successor RUN-260916-036865 immediately; resume is now explicitly authorized with changed prerequisite scope. Preserve exact two-file mapper/test delta from results. Reuse the already independently accepted scheme fixture correction from CR-BUG-260908-shki8p rev2, not a newly invented fix. Read its exact patch and review-verdict-rev2.md; verify the prerequisite bytes and missing/extra/combined negative cases. Add only the existing accepted fixture correction needed for this old-base managed gate, which was similarly used by shki8p. Current PR6 already carries it plus diagnostic runner calls, so downstream composition MUST change only the mapper/test pair and MUST NOT overwrite current PR fixture with an old-base full file. Inspect mise.toml then trust this task-scoped known config if safe; no installation or global trust. Rerun relevant gate and publish next CR through normal handoff; preserve normal review/checks. No other product/tooling scope expansion. Document this prerequisite explicitly in results and scope. If another unrelated validation failure surfaces, attach exact evidence and route blocked without repeated identical handoff attempts. Keep old candidate, logs, and all signed refs; no commits on managed branch, no VPN actions. The parent review brief applies to the reviewer, not producer; producer owns no accept_cr.\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `BUG-260916-20xt79_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(BUG-260916-20xt79, name=BUG-260916-20xt79_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `to-review` is a role handoff, not accepted completion. Report **ready for review** or **handed off to review**.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff BUG-260916-20xt79 --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Us