{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cf9f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a9c6-18e8-73c2-87df-807f8e977157"},"sequence":1578,"recorded_at":1780531400003151,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7f8b7742-5a98-412e-8203-1d9787ac5c82","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7f8b7742-5a98-412e-8203-1d9787ac5c82","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7f8b7742-5a98-412e-8203-1d9787ac5c82"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a9d2-e7ef-7f23-ad36-9fc24c71d81d"},"task_id":"01a0a9d2-e7ef-7f23-ad36-9fc24c71d81d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a9d2-e7ef-7f23-ad36-9fc24c71d81d","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-63-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board spawn --help 2>&1 | sed -n '40,120p'\",\n  \"description\": \"See remaining spawn help\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"                      helpful message if not found.\\n\\nPrompt file is auto-saved to .temp/prompts/ with timestamp naming.\\n\\nModel and reasoning selection:\\n  --model is required for every spawn of a role without a configured default.\\n  --reasoning-effort is required for Codex spawns.\\n  --reasoning-effort is required for Qwen spawns.\\n  --reasoning-effort is required for Claude spawns, except claude-haiku-4-5\\n  (and its dated snapshot), which take no effort at all.\\n  task-board never supplies model or reasoning defaults of its own. The only\\n  exception is a per-role default the project configured explicitly at\\n  spawn.ceilings.<provider>.roles.<role>.default_model and\\n  .default_reasoning_effort. That seed fills only the dimensions omitted at the\\n  callsite, an explicit flag always wins per dimension, and the seeded pair\\n  still passes the ordinary ceiling, so a default can never widen a bound. A\\n  role with no configured default keeps explicit selection mandatory. Inspect\\n  what a role resolves to before spawning with:\\n    task-board q 'project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=PROVIDER)'\\n  Inspect the current registry with: task-board q 'models(agent=codex)'\\n\\n  With model_criterion less_or_equal or greater_or_equal, every spawn also\\n  requires --selection-rationale with one non-empty line explaining the chosen\\n  pair. If policy changes the requested pair, spawn records the requested-pair\\n  rationale tuple in task notes, creates no run, and reports requested ->\\n  resolved. Re-evaluate the resolved pair, then either re-request within\\n  bounds/escalate or re-invoke with --ack-resolved <model>/<effort> matching it\\n  exactly and fresh rationale text. After whitespace normalization that text\\n  must differ byte-for-byte from every rationale already recorded for the task\\n  and role. Pass-through ordered selections do not use --ack-resolved.\\n  model_criterion equal uses neither flag and forbids selection assessments.\\n\\n  spawn-policy-v3 uses the admitted (model, effort) pair set as the sole\\n  admission authority; allowed_models and entries are two mutually exclusive\\n  input forms that both translate into it, and neither is itself the\\n  authority. spawn-policy-v4 is the identical wire shape under a new\\n  contract_version spelling -- the version v2 migration guidance now targets --\\n  and everything below applies to it unchanged.\\n  PolicyRank, registry order, lifecycle, and recommendation never change that\\n  set; an ordered entry consults capability rank only against an\\n  operator-approved entries_expansion_digest. An out-of-set model is refused, or resolved to the exact configured\\n  resolution_model. adjustment_confirmation=required uses the rationale/ack\\n  boundary above; none forbids both flags. Inspect the target-effective policy\\n  with project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=PROVIDER).\\n  Grandfathered v2 ordered and effort-only policies use the frozen compatibility\\n  snapshot. Their project_config migration objects are read-only; task-board\\n  never rewrites repository config automatically.\\n\\n  Optimize maximum task quality per token: assess scope, complexity, risk,\\n  required autonomy, validation burden, and expected context and token cost before launch.\\n  For board-managed Codex work, max is the highest recommended effort. ultra\\n  remains compatible on supported models but adds model-internal delegation;\\n  prefer task-board roles, RUN lifecycle, dependencies, and reviewer routing\\n  for predictable delegation.\\n\\nWorkload-aware recommendations:\\n  When spawn.workload_classes is configured, first query the target\\n  spawn-preflight with task_class=... or workload_class=.... Reason from the\\n  returned available pairs, ranking, provenance, dropped reasons, and snapshot.\\n  Then explicitly spawn with exactly one of --workload-task-class or\\n  --workload-class, plus the exact --recommendation-snapshot-digest and one\\n  non-empty --recommendation-rationale line. The selected available pair may\\n  follow or consciously reject the ranking. A recommendation never supplies a\\n  missing model/effort, widens authority, or auto-selects a pair.\\n\\nExamples:\\n  # Queue a Codex run with an explicit model and reasoning choice\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max\\n\\n  # Workload-aware explicit selection after a matching spawn-preflight query\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-luna --reasoning-effort high --workload-task-class code --recommendation-snapshot-digest sha256:... --recommendation-rationale \\\"Bounded implementation; Luna retains every validation gate\\\"\\n\\n  # Validate instruction resource is linked before spawning\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max --instruction impl-guide.md\\n\\n  # Spawn with specific model and budget\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent claude --model claude-opus-5 --budget 5.0 \\\\\\n    --instruction impl-guide.md\\n\\n  # Queue a balanced Codex model with an explicit effort\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-terra --reasoning-effort max\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5270,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1318,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
