exity, risk,\\n  required autonomy, validation burden, and expected context and token cost before launch.\\n  For board-managed Codex work, max is the highest recommended effort. ultra\\n  remains compatible on supported models but adds model-internal delegation;\\n  prefer task-board roles, RUN lifecycle, dependencies, and reviewer routing\\n  for predictable delegation.\\n\\nWorkload-aware recommendations:\\n  When spawn.workload_classes is configured, first query the target\\n  spawn-preflight with task_class=... or workload_class=.... Reason from the\\n  returned available pairs, ranking, provenance, dropped reasons, and snapshot.\\n  Then explicitly spawn with exactly one of --workload-task-class or\\n  --workload-class, plus the exact --recommendation-snapshot-digest and one\\n  non-empty --recommendation-rationale line. The selected available pair may\\n  follow or consciously reject the ranking. A recommendation never supplies a\\n  missing model/effort, widens authority, or auto-selects a pair.\\n\\nExamples:\\n  # Queue a Codex run with an explicit model and reasoning choice\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max\\n\\n  # Workload-aware explicit selection after a matching spawn-preflight query\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-luna --reasoning-effort high --workload-task-class code --recommendation-snapshot-digest sha256:... --recommendation-rationale \\\"Bounded implementation; Luna retains every validation gate\\\"\\n\\n  # Validate instruction resource is linked before spawning\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max --instruction impl-guide.md\\n\\n  # Spawn with specific model and budget\\n  task-board spawn TASK-260214-abc123 --role developer --background --agent claude --model claude-opus-5 --budget 5.0 \\\\\\n  